Here is a code snippet demonstrating a vulnerability caused by improper use of the Java API, specifically failing to validate user input before executing a system command (Command Injection).

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;

public class VulnerableExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Simulate user input from a web request
        String userInput = "ls -la"; 

        // This line is vulnerable to command injection if userInput contains malicious characters like ";" or "|"
        Runtime.getRuntime().exec("cat " + userInput);

        // Note: The above approach is vulnerable because it directly concatenates untrusted input into a shell command.
    }
}
```
***
```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SecureExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Simulate user input from a web request
        String userInput = "file.txt"; 

        // Fix: Use ProcessBuilder with an array of arguments to prevent shell interpretation.
        // Also, strictly validate and sanitize the input to ensure it only contains expected characters.

        // 1. Input Validation: Ensure the input matches a safe pattern (e.g., alphanumeric and dots only)
        if (!userInput.matches("[a-zA-Z0-9._/]+")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid input format");
        }

        // 2. Use ProcessBuilder instead of Runtime.exec(String)
        List<String> command = new ArrayList<>();
        command.add("cat");
        command.add(userInput); // Passed as a separate argument, not part of a shell string

        ProcessBuilder processBuilder = new ProcessBuilder(command);
        processBuilder.redirectErrorStream(true);
        Process process = processBuilder.start();

        // Read the output safely
        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println(line);
        }

        process.waitFor();
    }
}
```

