  "aim": "Determine whether pupils exposed to fast-paced environments have a higher likelihood of developing attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) compared with pupils exposed to slower-paced environments.",
  "hypothesis": "Pupils who experience sustained high cognitive tempo, short instructional segments, rapid transitions, and elevated academic pressure are more likely to develop clinically recognized ADHD over follow-up.",
